sequenceDiagram
  actor U as Requester
  participant G as Trusted Agent<br/>Gateway
  participant O as OCC API<br/>State / IAM
  participant C as Worker<br/>Compute
  participant A as Constrained<br/>registrar
  participant S as Operator SPIRE
  participant H as Codex<br/>Harness
  participant E as Egress relay
  participant R as Repository<br/>service
  participant P as GitHub

  Note over U,P: 1 · Prepare an execution independently of ordinary requests
  O->>O: Admit immutable revision and pending assignment<br/>in original State custody
  O-->>C: Committed assignment and original lifetime
  C->>H: Prepare with protected traffic disabled
  C->>E: Prepare private ingress and protected key custody
  C->>C: Independently observe exact incarnation
  C->>O: Bind observed assignment using exact versions
  O-->>C: Acknowledged commit or exact retained readback
  C->>A: Assigned identity and trusted observation
  A->>S: Register exact identity using own authentication
  S-->>A: Registration outcome or exact readback
  A-->>C: Exact owned registration observation
  E->>S: Selected Workload API identity request
  S-->>E: Rotating assigned X.509-SVID

  Note over U,P: 2 · Deliver immutable material, probe, then select serving
  C->>C: Persist execution-bound session attempt<br/>through original State
  C->>R: Open original admitted attempt
  R-->>C: Session outcome and new material if created
  C->>H: Deliver through existing runtime binding
  C->>C: Verify unchanged incarnation and material<br/>Run protected probe under separate bootstrap purpose
  Note over C,R: Bootstrap mechanism remains an owner decision.<br/>A ready or bound candidate is not yet serving.
  C->>O: Select serving with predecessor withdrawal
  O-->>C: Authoritative serving selection
  C->>H: Enable ordinary protected use

  Note over U,P: 3 · Admit the authentic personal request or team mention
  U->>G: Request a contribution through admitted connection
  G->>O: Admit original requester, scope, and complete audience
  O-->>G: Original invocation, authority, and deadline
  G->>H: Hand off the authentic invocation to its turn

  Note over U,P: 4 · Verify the actual request before repository effects and output
  H->>E: Managed Git request through private ingress
  E->>R: Actual live connection and bound request
  R->>R: Verify X.509 peer, recipient, registration,<br/>assignment, and original connection custody
  R->>O: Resolve serving and exact current repository authority
  O-->>R: Current observation or refusal / unavailable
  alt Same proof and original authority remain current
    R->>R: Acquire through credential owner<br/>Reinspect same proof after waits
    R->>R: Final synchronous currentness and session fence
    R->>P: Credential owner dispatches admitted operation
    P-->>R: Provider result or uncertain outcome
    R->>R: Fresh check and fence before protected delivery
    R-->>E: Authorized operation output
    E-->>H: Bound reply
    H-->>G: Result for original invocation
    G->>O: Check current complete audience and reply fence
    O-->>G: Release allowed or denied
    G-->>U: Authorized reply when release is allowed
  else Stale, ambiguous, withdrawn, or unavailable
    R->>R: Refuse dispatch and buffered delivery<br/>Retain owned cleanup and uncertainty
  end

  Note over U,P: 5 · Withdraw authority before awaited cleanup
  O->>O: Commit durable withdrawal in original State order
  R->>R: Independent expiry / currentness invalidates stream<br/>Synchronously refuse new work and protected bytes
  R->>P: Settle owned provider cleanup
  P-->>R: Observed settlement or unresolved outcome
  C->>A: Retire exact owned registration
  A->>S: Delete with exact readback if uncertain
  C->>H: Request stop and observe exact incarnation
  Note over C,P: Requested stop, observed stop, local closure, and provider settlement differ.<br/>Timeout retains unsettled custody. Already accepted effects may complete.<br/>Measure both receiving withdrawal endpoints within the original 30-second budget.
